- id: 421a_tax_abatement
  name: 421-a Tax Abatement
  description: A state tax incentive for new construction that requires rent-stabilization
    protections for tenants during the abatement period.
  jurisdiction: NYS
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id001 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.metcouncilonhousing.org/help-answers/about-rent-stabilization/
    sample_quotes:
    - 421-a tax abatements (for new construction) and a J-51 tax abatements (for upgrades
      to existing buildings) give rent-stabilization protections to tenants otherwise
      not covered
    suggested_aliases: *id001
  citation: NY RPTL § 421-a
- id: 421a_tax_exemption_law
