- id: dhcr_regulation_on_fraud
  name: DHCR Regulation on Fraud
  description: A regulation allowing the DHCR to examine the rental history of an
    apartment for up to four years prior to a complaint if the landlord is found to
    have committed fraud.
  jurisdiction: NYS
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id003 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/2759844/corsini-v-morgan/
    sample_quotes:
    - The regulation permits the DHCR to look back beyond the four-year statute of
      limitations in cases of fraud.
    suggested_aliases: *id003
  citation: 9 NYCRR § 2526.1(a)
