- id: fair_housing_act_title_viii
  name: Fair Housing Act (Title VIII of the Civil Rights Act of 1968)
  description: Federal law prohibiting discrimination in the sale, rental, financing,
    and other housing-related transactions based on race, color, national origin,
    religion, sex, familial status, and disability.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id006
  - Fair Housing Act (42 U.S.C. § 3601 et seq.)
  - Fair Housing Act (Federal)
  - Federal Fair Housing Act
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.justfix.org/en/learn/air-conditioning-laws
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/8716132/smith-v-housing-authority/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/10679704/walker-v-us-department-of-agriculture-rural-development/
    - https://www.metcouncilonhousing.org/help-answers/housing-discrimination/
    sample_quotes:
    - The Fair Housing Act was referenced in the discrimination claim.
    - City, State, and Federal Fair Housing laws require landlords to make reasonable
      accommodations, including potentially upgrading electric systems to allow for
      air conditioning installations.
    - Title VIII of the Civil Rights Act of 1968 (Fair Housing Act), as amended, prohibits
      discrimination in the sale, rental, and financing of dwellings, and in other
      housing-related transactions, based on race, color, national origin, religion,
      sex, familial status (including children under the age of 18 living with parents
      or legal custodians, pregnant women, and people securing custody of children
      under the age of 18), and diability.
    suggested_aliases: *id006
  citation: 42 U.S.C. § 3601 et seq.
