- id: vacancy_increase_law
  name: Vacancy Increase Law
  description: A law allowing landlords to raise rent by up to 20% when a new tenant
    moves into a rent-stabilized apartment, prior to June 2019.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id055 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.metcouncilonhousing.org/help-answers/rent-stabilization-overcharges/
    sample_quotes:
    - Prior to June of 2019, landlords automatically get to raise rents 20% when a
      new tenant moves in.
    suggested_aliases: *id055
  citation: NYC Admin Code § 26-511(c)(5)
